---
source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons install-completions -h <==
Install the completion script where your shell looks for it

Usage: omaddons install-completions [OPTIONS] <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>  The shell to install the completion script for [possible values: bash, zsh, fish, elvish,
           powershell]

Options:
      --force  Replace a completion file omaddons did not write

Examples:
  omaddons install-completions bash           where bash-completion looks
  omaddons install-completions zsh --dry-run  where it would write, and what

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons install-completions --help <==
Install the completion script where your shell looks for it

For bash, zsh or fish: the script completions prints, written to the shell's own folder. Run it
again after upgrading.

Usage: omaddons install-completions [OPTIONS] <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>
          The shell to install the completion script for
          
          [possible values: bash, zsh, fish, elvish, powershell]

Options:
      --force
          Replace a completion file omaddons did not write
          
          Without it, a file at the shell's location that lacks omaddons' marker line is refused and
          left as it is. A symlink there is refused even with --force.

Examples:
  omaddons install-completions bash             for bash, with bash-completion
  omaddons install-completions zsh --dry-run    where it would write, and what
  omaddons install-completions fish --force     replace a script it did not write

Writes the script omaddons completions prints, with a marker line, where each shell looks
for your own completions: bash in $XDG_DATA_HOME/bash-completion/completions/omaddons
(default ~/.local/share), zsh in ~/.zfunc/_omaddons, and fish in
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fish/completions/omaddons.fish (default ~/.config). The folder above
those (the data or config folder, or your home) must exist; the ones below it are
created. When it creates ~/.zfunc, add fpath+=("$HOME/.zfunc") to .zshrc before
compinit. A file without the marker is never replaced unless --force is given, and a
symlink never is. Run it again after upgrading omaddons; elvish and PowerShell load
completions from their rc files, which omaddons does not edit: see README's "Shell
completions".

See also: completions

Global options:
      --json             One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>  The client to act on: id, game mode, family, path, or all [alias: --flavor]
      --dry-run          Show the plan without changing anything
      --actor <ACTOR>    Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>    Why, recorded verbatim in history
      --offline          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running    Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --no-color         No ANSI color
      --no-progress      No progress output
      --progress <MODE>  Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet            Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...       More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help             Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
